{{also|kartoffel}}
==German==
{{wikipedia|lang=de}}

===Etymology===
{{borrowing|it|tartuficolo|t=[[truffle]]|lang=de}}, from {{etyl|ML.|de}} {{m|la|*territūberum}}.<ref>{{R:EWddS|hw=Kartoffel|ed=22}}</ref>

The use as an ethnic nickname is due to the prominence of potatoes in German cuisine, particularly vis-à-vis the cuisines of the major allochthone communities in the country. (Compare the corresponding {{m|de|Spagetti}} used to refer to Italians.)

